    <detaileddescription>
<para>allocation <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">cslt::HeapAllocator<sp/>allocator;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">auto<sp/>result1<sp/>=<sp/>allocator.alloc(1024,<sp/>false);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">void*<sp/>ptr<sp/>=<sp/>result1.value();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">//<sp/>Shrink<sp/>to<sp/>512<sp/>bytes</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">auto<sp/>result2<sp/>=<sp/>allocator.realloc(ptr,<sp/>1024,<sp/>512,<sp/>false);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">if<sp/>(result2.hasValue())<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>void*<sp/>new_ptr<sp/>=<sp/>result2.value();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>//<sp/>First<sp/>512<sp/>bytes<sp/>preserved</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>allocator.return_element(new_ptr,<sp/>512,<sp/>allocator.default_alignment());</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>After calling realloc, the original pointer is invalid. Always use the newly returned pointer.</para>
</simplesect>
